        <h1>
            How to Choose the Right Rental Car
        </h1>

    </section>


    <main class="blog-container">

        <img
            src="/images/blog-2.jpg"
            alt="Choose Rental Car"
            class="blog-image"
        >

        <div class="blog-content">

            <p>
                Choosing the right rental car can make a major
                difference to your travel experience. The perfect
                vehicle depends on your destination, budget,
                passengers, luggage, and driving requirements.
            </p>

            <h2>1. Consider Your Trip Type</h2>

            <p>
                Think about where you are travelling. A small sedan
                can be ideal for city driving, while an SUV may be
                better for highways, family trips, or rougher roads.
            </p>

            <h2>2. Check Passenger Capacity</h2>

            <p>
                Make sure the car has enough seats for everyone.
                Also consider luggage space, especially if you are
                travelling with multiple passengers.
            </p>

            <h2>3. Set Your Budget</h2>

            <p>
                Decide your daily rental budget before choosing a
                vehicle. Remember to consider fuel, taxes, deposits,
                insurance, and other possible charges.
            </p>

            <h2>4. Choose the Transmission</h2>

            <p>
                Automatic cars are generally convenient for city
                traffic, while manual cars may be preferred by drivers
                who enjoy greater control.
            </p>

            <h2>5. Consider Fuel Type</h2>

            <p>
                Petrol, diesel, hybrid, and electric vehicles can have
                different running costs. Choose the fuel type according
                to your route and available charging or fuel stations.
            </p>

            <h2>Final Tip</h2>

            <p>
                The best rental car is not always the most expensive
                one. Choose a vehicle that matches your actual travel
                needs, passenger count, comfort requirements, and
                budget.
            </p>

